    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#333] mt-10 mb-3" style="font-family:'Trebuchet MS',Trebuchet,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif">Verification notes</h2>
    <div class="text-base text-[#555]">
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 my-3"><li>Dollar-denominated "global HVAC market size" aggregates from commercial research round-ups were excluded: no producing primary source publishes a single audited figure. Unit demand (JRAIA) and audited manufacturer revenue (Daikin) are used as market-scale measures instead.</li><li>The two IEA 2050 projections are different report vintages, not a contradiction: the 2022 Space Cooling tracker projects "more than double" under current policy; the 2018 <em>Future of Cooling</em> projected "more than triple" without efficiency action.</li><li>The AHRI November 2024 monthly/year-to-date figures predate the verified full-year 2025 release and are kept as distinct, period-labelled datapoints.</li><li>Where a figure is regional (Europe heat pump sales, U.S. shipments and wages, Hong Kong energy use), the geography is stated with the number.</li></ul>
    </div>
